Subject: Restrict Hans IPC entrypoints in the built kernel, without a framework overlay

Target: Ace 6 common c1802dd6f3343e71c166a3c67c50554c81880b6e, Android 16
framework a4308e9fe612f25770417c751e47f0fee94e92987069e30d87f707b87b2e8f37.

Only UID 1000 may connect to the exact abstract hans_socket_server endpoint
or invoke listener registration/unregistration (codes 3/4) on the exact
com.oplus.app.IOplusHansFreezeManager interface in system_server. The installed
Oplus Wi-Fi monitor and native hans client both run as UID 1000.

Binder checks the completed kernel buffer after deferred copies and before
queueing; failures use existing transaction cleanup. Other interfaces,
methods, replies and Unix names retain their existing LSM checks. This does
not implement Java signature permission checks or change any SELinux rules,
module ABI, userspace JAR, Root/BL status or event contents.

